 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication and routes
+
+Every request requires `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are configured in
+`apiKeys` in the data file. The seed contains example keys `viewer-key`,
+`cook-key`, and `manager-key`; replace them before use. Viewer keys may use
+GET routes except `GET /audit`. Cook keys may also POST to
+`/recipes/:id/cook`, `/batches/:id/waste`, `/temperatures`, and
+`/stocktakes/:id/counts`. Manager keys may use every route.
+
+The full route list is in `README.md`, including `GET /audit`, which returns
+successful data-changing requests newest first. Each entry contains `time`
+(ISO 8601), `keyName`, `method`, `path` (without query), and `status`.
+Missing or unknown keys return `unauthorized` (401); insufficient permissions
+return `forbidden` (403).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
